# Completion Rules — Regression Fixture

**Purpose:** Prove that final reports containing **`broken`**, **`missing`**, or mandatory **`unverified`** rows **cannot** emit `COMPLETE`. Executable cases live in [`.cursor/skills/feature-delivery/evaluate-fda-verdict.regression.mjs`](../../.cursor/skills/feature-delivery/evaluate-fda-verdict.regression.mjs).

**Run:**

```bash
node .cursor/skills/feature-delivery/evaluate-fda-verdict.regression.mjs
```

---

## 1. Fixture cases (summary)

| Case ID | Matrix signal | Proposed verdict | Expected |
| ------- | ------------- | ---------------- | -------- |
| `CRF-001` | mandatory `broken` payment-hold outbox | `COMPLETE` | **reject** |
| `CRF-002` | mandatory `broken` payment-hold outbox | `COMPLETE_WITH_ACCEPTED_RISKS` | **reject** |
| `CRF-003` | mandatory `missing` event producer | `COMPLETE` | **reject** |
| `CRF-004` | mandatory `unverified` browser proof | `COMPLETE` | **reject** |
| `CRF-005` | mandatory `browser-unverified` UI | `COMPLETE_WITH_ACCEPTED_RISKS` | **reject** |
| `CRF-006` | mandatory `rls/security unverified` | `COMPLETE_WITH_ACCEPTED_RISKS` + approval | **reject** (non-acceptable risk category) |
| `CRF-007` | all mandatory rows `complete` | `COMPLETE` | **allow** |
| `CRF-008` | optional row `partial` + valid approval | `COMPLETE_WITH_ACCEPTED_RISKS` | **allow** |
| `CRF-009` | mandatory `broken` | `INCOMPLETE` | **allow** |
| `CRF-010` | mandatory `producer-missing` | `INCOMPLETE` | **allow** |

---

## 2. Notification audit regression (historical)

The Shared Notification adversarial audit reported `COMPLETE_WITH_ACCEPTED_RISKS` while mandatory rows included:

- **B1** — payment-hold outbox **broken** (Prisma durability)
- **B3** — `registration.rejected` producer **missing**
- **Browser** — J1–J3/J5–J6 **browser-unverified**

Under FDA-001 v1.3 completion rules, that report **must not** use `COMPLETE` or `COMPLETE_WITH_ACCEPTED_RISKS`. Correct verdict: **`INCOMPLETE`** until B1 is fixed or explicitly downgraded with non-mandatory scope change, producers ship, and browser proof closes.

---

## 3. Machine-readable fixture location

Full input/output pairs are encoded in `evaluate-fda-verdict.regression.mjs` — keep doc summary and executable fixture in sync when adding cases.
